# The PrismPM revision `prismpm build` is made by in .github/workflows/lexlean.yml,
# the only place it is written (AGENTS.md R1), like .github/lexlean.rev. The
# workflow builds `prismpm` at this commit and builds the conformance server
# application with it (conformance/, prismpm.toml).
#
# The LexLean it is built with is not the one PrismPM vendors but the revision of
# .github/lexlean.rev, so one pin drives both tools: the vendored lexlean (e0b74b81e,
# the v0.4.0 tag) lacks SM-37, and `JsonWriteLaws` uses `nested_induction`, which
# only SM-37 and later has. Nothing in PrismPM changes; the workflow replaces
# vendor/lexlean in its own copy of the tree (.github/lexlean-ci/lib.sh, `install_prismpm`; CI.md).
#
# The pin moves to the PrismPM SDK release before MCP v0.1.0, and that release must
# pin a LexLean release that contains SM-37.
#
# Currently: PrismPM main at 585ee8eb3 (version 0.4.0), whose workspace requires
# lexlean 0.4.0, the version of .github/lexlean.rev; #339 (version 0.3.0) cannot
# take it.
rev = 585ee8eb3123e624a189edbcba1001b6b7c57855
